From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: k114s-integration <integration@localhost>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 09:51:02 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] drm/apple: K114s: no panel EDR above 500 nits by default

The K114s kernel is built for one machine, whose OLED panel's ADT
gives a 2000 nit peak. Nobody has shown PQ content on a K-board OLED
under this driver, so the K114s build starts with
fw27_panel_edr_max_nits at 500. With the panel's SDR maximum of 1000
nits that leaves no headroom: the panel offers no EDR, its EDID
advertises no PQ, and PQ commits are refused. SDR brightness is not
affected. Setting the parameter on the kernel command line or in
modprobe.d raises the cap once EDR is to be tested.

K114s-only: not for upstream, where the default stays 0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c
index d4684f5a65..e332f414f0 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c
@@ -1181,10 +1181,10 @@ static void dcp_panel_read_min_brightness(struct apple_dcp *dcp,
  * headroom, so the panel offers no EDR at all: its EDID advertises no PQ and
  * PQ commits are refused.  Read once, when the display processor binds.
  */
-static unsigned int fw27_panel_edr_max_nits;
+static unsigned int fw27_panel_edr_max_nits = 500;	/* K114s build */
 module_param(fw27_panel_edr_max_nits, uint, 0444);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(fw27_panel_edr_max_nits,
-		 "Firmware 27 panels: most nits an EDR swap may ask for, 0 for the panel's peak (default: 0)");
+		 "Firmware 27 panels: most nits an EDR swap may ask for, 0 for the panel's peak (default: 500)");
 
 static void dcp_panel_read_adt(struct apple_dcp *dcp)
 {
